P["33492b75-fedc-44b9-b85d-165064aa1d7e"] = [  # returning local address
    "A local array has automatic storage: it lives in the function's stack frame, which is released on return.",
    "The returned pointer is dangling; later calls reuse that stack memory, so reads give garbage or crash: undefined behaviour.",
    "Fix 1: allocate with malloc and return the pointer; the caller owns it and must free it (flexible size, risk of leaks).",
    "Fix 2: the caller passes in a buffer and its size; the function fills it (no allocation, clear ownership, caller must size it).",
    "(static local array also works but is shared between calls and not thread-safe.)",
    "AddressSanitizer detects stack-use-after-return and out-of-bounds accesses at run time; Valgrind memcheck reports invalid reads/writes, leaks and use of uninitialised memory.",
]
